{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Science, Old and New"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "What is Anthropology?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le15ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Modals for Possibility and Certainty "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use modals to talk about degrees of certainty.<br/><br/>You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "  You can use <span class=\"italic\">must</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">may</span>,  <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, and  <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to describe degrees of certainty."}, {"type": "text", "content": "  Must = it's very likely <br/> Must not / Could not / Can't = it's not possible<br/> May / Might / Can / Could = it's possible<br/> May not / Might not = it's possible this is not true"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You may wonder where anthropological studies began.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible that you wonder.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">It might surprise you that originally, it was part of natural history and the study of animals.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It possible that this will surprise you.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> They might look at the connections between holiday customs and religious beliefs. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible that they will look at those particular connections.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> These connections could allow them to shed light on what makes us different and what makes us the same. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible that we may get some insight.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You may not find this anthropology class very interesting.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible that you will not find this interesting.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Present Perfect Tense vs. Past Simple "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way. <br/><br/>You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event  <span class=\"strong\">not</span> necessarily connected to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "To help you decide whether you should use the Present Perfect tense or the Past Simple tense, ask yourself the questions \u2018When?'"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you can answer the question \"When?\", the past time is stated or inferred or understood. Use the Past Simple. There is no connection to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "If the you cannot answer the question \"When?\", because the time is not stated or not important, then choose the Present Perfect tense. There is instead a connection to the present."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sentence\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" When?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Have you ever wondered what humans were like long ago? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" at any time from the past to now\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Now, anthropology has become more like a social science. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  from the past to now\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> At first, anthropologists mainly studied non-Western cultures and peoples. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" when they first started\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Physical anthropology began to look at how our species, homo sapiens, evolved.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" when it became something to study\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Have you thought about what life is like in other cultures? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Recently, many new branches of anthropology have developed."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Of course the change in approach brought a change in method."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Urban anthropology opened studies on human experiences and social relations in urban areas. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "anthropological"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "concerned with the study of the origin and development of humans"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You may wonder where anthropological studies began. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about anthropology."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "anthropology"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the study of human societies, customs, and beliefs"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are questions raised in anthropology - the science that studies human beings."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "natural history"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the study of living things and their natural environments"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Originally, anthropology was part of natural history and the study of animals."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "social science"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the study of the way that people live in society"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Anthropology has become more like a social science."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob01aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "branch"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that develops or derives from a principal source or origin"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Recently, many new branches of anthropology have developed. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob01aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "artifact"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an object produced or shaped by human craft, especially a tool or a  weapon"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Like other scientists, anthropologists collected artifacts."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "in conjunction with"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "combined with"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: By studying customs in conjunction with these artifacts, they were able to create pictures of past societies."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "urban"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "relating to towns and cities, or happening there"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Urban anthropology opened studies on human experiences and social relations in urban areas."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob01aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to shed light on"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make something clearer "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: These connections could allow anthropologists to shed light on what makes us different and what makes us the same. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le15ob01aud09"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look up your country and anthropology together."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find out about a people that lived in your country in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make notes on where they lived, what they looked like and what they did."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find out what they have left behind. Is it pottery, art, traditions?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Now write 120 words in two paragraphs - one for the past and one for the time up to now."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your paragraphs to a partner. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss what you have told them."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about peopl