": [], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}}], "id": 10}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "engenn8le15ob01re7pdf01.pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "DWS", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nFind out about people from the past in your country.\n"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n"}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 11}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn8le15ob01re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": "engenn8le15ob01re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "100", "text": "Have you ever wondered what humans were like long ago? Have you thought about what life is like in other cultures? These are questions raised in anthropology - the science that studies human beings. You may wonder where anthropological studies began. It might surprise you that originally, it was part of natural history and the study of animals.", "id": 1, "image": "engenn8le15ob01re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "23000", "text": "<p>At first, anthropologists mainly studied non-Western cultures and peoples. Of course, like other scientists, they collected artifacts. By studying customs in conjunction with these artifacts, they were, in fact, able to create pictures of past societies.</p>\n<p>Now, anthropology has become more like a social science. Of course the change in approach brought a change in method. In fact, now, anthropologists look for connections between various aspects of society rather than just the way it's organized. For example, they might look at the connections between holiday customs and religious beliefs.</p>", "id": 2, "image": "engenn8le15ob01re2img02.jpg"}, {"time": "64000", "text": "<p>Recently, many new branches of anthropology have developed. Physical anthropology began to look at how our species, homo sapiens, evolved. Urban anthropology opened studies on human experiences and social relations in urban areas.</p>\n<p>Of course, no matter which branch of anthropology they work in, the goal of anthropologists is to find patterns and connections. These connections could allow them to shed light on what makes us different and what makes us the same.</p>", "id": 3, "image": "engenn8le15ob01re2img03.jpg"}], "coverimg": "engenn8le15ob01re2img01.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": [], "title": ""}], "id": 0}]}